# Wave W17-Q (Route 120): rain barrel — a Weather Institute rain barrel standing by the road: banded wooden staves under a pale disc of caught rainwater, one of the barrels the Institute logs this route’s rain by (design: the lake keeps a scorched secret; the cliff keeps a sealed one — and the Institute logs the rain by the barrel; the barrels objected). On ledger turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — the fleet’s only barrel: split from Route 119’s gauge boxes by form (coopered wood and open water vs the Institute’s lidded instrument box).
